# SECTION 01 — PURPOSE

## Purpose

The purpose of Phase-06 is to establish the Workbench Architecture of the COREI Institutional Operator Workstation.

The Workbench is the software architecture that transforms constitutional principles, operator workflows, operational environments, behavioural models, and governed technologies into one unified institutional operating environment.

It is not a frontend application.

It is not a dashboard.

It is not a browser page.

It is not a window manager.

It is the operational foundation upon which every institutional capability executes.

The Workbench provides the common runtime that hosts:

* operational workspaces,
* institutional intelligence,
* workflow engines,
* environmental services,
* operator context,
* command systems,
* extension capabilities,
* visual composition,
* operational orchestration.

Every professional operator interacts with the institution through the Workbench.

The Workbench itself remains largely invisible.

Operators interact with institutional reality.

The Workbench continuously manages the environment behind the scenes.

---

# SECTION 02 — MISSION

## Mission

The mission of the Workbench is to provide one coherent software architecture capable of supporting every institutional capability throughout years of continuous evolution.

The Workbench shall become the permanent operating foundation for COREI.

Its mission includes providing:

* environmental composition,
* workspace lifecycle,
* layout orchestration,
* capability hosting,
* contextual awareness,
* operator sessions,
* institutional state,
* command execution,
* extension management,
* service coordination,
* runtime governance.

Unlike traditional applications, the Workbench does not implement business functionality.

Instead, it provides the environment within which business capabilities operate.

Consistent with the COREI Anchor Law, the Workbench exists to make institutional operation coherent rather than fragmented.

Consistent with the Master Trader Persona, the Workbench should disappear behind professional operation, allowing disciplined analysis, investigation, execution, and continuous operational awareness to remain central.

The success of the Workbench is therefore measured by institutional coherence rather than visible software features.

