# SECTION 03 — PROBLEM STATEMENT

## Problem Statement

Traditional enterprise software typically evolves through independent applications.

Each application introduces:

* its own navigation,
* its own state,
* its own notifications,
* its own search,
* its own permissions,
* its own workflows.

As capability increases, the operator experiences fragmentation.

Even when individual applications perform well, the institution becomes operationally disconnected.

For COREI this approach is unacceptable.

The Institutional Operator Workstation must support:

* hundreds of capabilities,
* dozens of intelligence engines,
* multiple terminals,
* multiple operational realities,
* AI systems,
* collaborative workflows,
* continuous institutional operation.

Without a Workbench Architecture, these capabilities inevitably become loosely connected software rather than one institutional operating environment.

The problem therefore is not building better components.

The problem is providing one architectural foundation through which every capability behaves as part of one institution.

Phase-06 solves this problem by defining the COREI Workbench.

