One recommendation before Phase-07

I would add one more constitutional principle that naturally emerges from everything we've built so far:

The Workbench owns the environment.

Capabilities own business behaviour.

Components own presentation.

Technologies own implementation.

This creates exceptionally clear architectural boundaries:

The Workbench never contains trading logic.
A Trading Capability never manages layouts or global navigation.
A Component never owns institutional workflows.
A Library never defines architecture.

That separation of responsibilities is, in my view, one of the strongest architectural characteristics of COREI and provides a durable foundation for the remaining phases of Stage-23.
